1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,920
In nineteen sixty-eight, a 3M chemist

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,940
tried to make an extremely strong glue,

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:05,720
and failed.

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,800
Spencer Silver had made the opposite.

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,980
A glue so weak, you could peel it off and

6
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:11,900
stick it back again.

7
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:13,440
Nobody wanted it.

8
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:15,700
For five years, he showed it to anyone

9
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,240
who'd listen.

10
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:18,740
Then a colleague, Art Fry, had a problem

11
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:19,300
